\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hark! the gospel news is sounding:
\par Christ hath suffered on the tree;
\par Streams of mercy are abounding;
\par Grace for all is rich and free.
\par Now, poor sinner,
\par Look to Him who died for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O escape to yonder mountain!
\par Now begin to watch and pray;
\par Christ invites you to the fountain,
\par Come, and wash your sins away:
\par Do not tarry,
\par Come to Jesus while you may.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Grace is flowing like a river;
\par Millions there have been supplied;
\par Still it flows as fresh as ever
\par From the Saviour's wounded side:
\par None need perish;
\par All may live, for Christ hath died.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Christ alone shall be our portion;
\par Soon we hope to meet above,
\par Then we'll bathe in the full ocean
\par Of the great Redeemer's love;
\par All His fullness,
\par We shall then for ever prove.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

